# Implementation Plan - Supabase Robustness Fix

The objective is to resolve the runtime crash caused by missing Supabase environment variables and provide a clear configuration path for the user.

## Proposed Changes

### [Supabase Utility]
#### [MODIFY] [server.ts](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/lib/supabase/server.ts)
- Add defensive checks for `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`.
- Log a clear error message if variables are missing instead of allowing a crash.
- Return `null` or a restricted client if initialization is not possible.

### [User Service]
#### [MODIFY] [users.service.ts](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/modules/users/users.service.ts)
- Wrap [getAuthenticatedUser](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/modules/users/users.service.ts#118-142) logic in a try/catch block.
- Ensure it gracefully returns `null` if the Supabase client cannot be initialized.

### [Configuration]
#### [NEW] [.env.example](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/.env.example)
- Define the required keys: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npx tsc --noEmit` to ensure no type regressions.

### Manual Verification
- Verify that the app loads even if `.env.local` is missing (Navbar will be hidden).
- Instruct the user to verify by filling in the keys.
